BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 790 Td (Each area has two questions. Positive and negative wording is scored in the correct direction.) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 777 Td (These are educational project questions inspired by the framework; they are not presented as) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 764 Td (official results from the licensed or official Areas of Worklife Survey.) Tj ET
BT /B 12 Tf 52 745 Td (Job Demands?Resources \(JD-R\) model) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 715 Td (The website uses the JD-R model to explain possible workplace patterns:) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 696 Td (- Job demands are pressures that require sustained effort, such as workload, deadlines,) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 683 Td (interruptions, emotional demands, or unclear expectations.) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 670 Td (- Job resources are supports that help a person manage work, such as autonomy, feedback,) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 657 Td (recognition, teamwork, fairness, and practical support.) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 638 Td (The model is used to explain why high demands and limited resources may make exhaustion harder) Tj ET
BT /R 9.2 Tf 52 625 Td (to manage. It is used for education and suggestions, not for diagnosis or proof of causation.) Tj ET
